// hello.golem
//
// Illustrative-only. The Golem language has no lexer/parser/compiler yet
// (src/ is still a placeholder - see docs/devlog/2026-07-28.md's "Next
// steps" checklist and AGENTS.md). This file exists purely to give the
// rest of this directory (program.asm, loader.asm) a source-level anchor:
// "if Golem could compile something today, this is the trivial program
// whose *compiled output* program.asm/program.bin hand-simulates."
//
// Syntax here is speculative/illustrative, drawn loosely from
// docs/design/language-type-proposals.md's tentative lean, and should NOT
// be treated as settled language design.

print "Hello, World! (via a simulated Golem-compiled buffer, not hand-written eZ80 assembly)"
